.TH BIGINTMULFFT 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntMul, bigIntMulFFT \- multiply dynamic integers exactly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

int bigIntMul(BigInt *result, const BigInt *a, const BigInt *b);
int bigIntMulFFT(BigInt *result, const BigInt *a, const BigInt *b);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Both functions multiply signed values, applying the product of operand signs.
Zero results are canonical positive zero; transforms operate on magnitudes.
.PP
Mul selects schoolbook when either input has fewer than 32 limbs; otherwise
it requests verified FFT. MulFFT uses base-256 complex convolution with exact
coefficient verification modulo 998244353 where its bounds hold.
.PP
Runtime checks require 4 * min(a.size,b.size) * 255^2 below the modulus and a
padded transform length at most 2^23. A shorter operand of at most 3837 limbs
satisfies the uniform coefficient bound; 3838 does not. Outside either bound,
multiplication uses an exact schoolbook fallback.
.PP
Incorrect or non-finite FFT coefficients recover from the NTT coefficients.
Supported transforms take O(n log n) time and O(n) scratch; the fallback is
quadratic. Output may alias either or both inputs. All objects must be
initialized. Products are published only after success.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0, -1 for allocation/transform failure, or INT_MAX for an unrepresentable
size. Errors leave output unchanged. Temporary allocations are released.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
